==Marketing==
[[File:1922 Gillette razor and blades advert, color.jpg|thumb|1922 advertisement for various New Improved and Old Type razor models]]

Gillette first introduced its long-time slogan, "The Best a Man Can Get", during a [[Super Bowl commercial|commercial]] first aired during [[Super Bowl XXIII]] in 1989.<ref name="adweek-bestmencanbe">{{Cite web|url=https://www.adweek.com/brand-marketing/gillette-asks-how-we-define-masculinity-in-the-metoo-era-as-the-best-a-man-can-get-turns-30/|title=Gillette Asks How We Define Masculinity in the #MeToo Era as 'The Best a Man Can Get' Turns 30|website=Adweek|date=14 January 2019 |language=en-US|access-date=2019-01-15|archive-date=2020-12-24|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201224042329/https://www.adweek.com/brand-marketing/gillette-asks-how-we-define-masculinity-in-the-metoo-era-as-the-best-a-man-can-get-turns-30/|url-status=live}}</ref> In 2024, singer [[Tom Grennan]] sang the song for a UK advert, and released it as a single.

The company has sponsored [[Major League Baseball]] (MLB),<ref>{{cite journal |last1=Lefton |first1=Terry |title=Gillette exits role as MLB's oldest sponsor |journal=New York Business Journal |date=April 12, 2018 |page=April 12, 2018 |url=https://www.bizjournals.com/newyork/news/2018/04/12/gillette-exits-role-as-mlb-s-oldest-sponsor.html |access-date=January 26, 2021 |archive-date=September 2, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210902005157/https://www.bizjournals.com/newyork/news/2018/04/12/gillette-exits-role-as-mlb-s-oldest-sponsor.html |url-status=live }}</ref> the [[2010 Gillette Fusion ProGlide 500]], and the [[Olympic Games]],<ref>{{cite news |last1=Bearne |first1=Suzanne |title=Gillette kicks off Olympics coaching campaign |url=https://www.marketingweek.com/gillette-kicks-off-olympics-coaching-campaign/ |access-date=January 26, 2021 |work=[[Marketing Week]] |date=May 14, 2012 |archive-date=September 2, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210902005130/https://www.marketingweek.com/gillette-kicks-off-olympics-coaching-campaign/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite journal |last1=Brayson |first1=Johnny |title=This Olympics Commercial Has A Powerful Message |url=https://www.bustle.com/articles/176805-the-athletes-in-gillettes-olympics-commercial-show-the-unseen-side-of-glory |website=[[Bustle (magazine)|Bustle]] |date=4 August 2016 |publisher=August 4, 2016 |access-date=January 26, 2021 |archive-date=September 28, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160928040456/http://www.bustle.com/articles/176805-the-athletes-in-gillettes-olympics-commercial-show-the-unseen-side-of-glory |url-status=live }}</ref> and has naming rights to [[Gillette Stadium]] in [[Foxborough, Massachusetts]], home venue for the [[National Football League]]'s [[New England Patriots]] and [[Major League Soccer]]'s [[New England Revolution]].<ref>{{cite news |title=CMGI Field is now Gillette Stadium |url=https://money.cnn.com/2002/08/05/news/companies/gillette/ |access-date=January 26, 2021 |work=[[CNN Money]] |publisher=[[CNN]] |date=August 5, 2002 |archive-date=February 2, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210202201905/https://money.cnn.com/2002/08/05/news/companies/gillette/ |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Gillette naming rights extended |url=https://www.espn.com/blog/boston/new-england-patriots/post/_/id/4683840/gillette-naming-rights-extended-through-2031 |date=September 22, 2010 |publisher=[[ESPN]] |access-date=January 26, 2021 |archive-date=March 3, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160303202108/http://espn.go.com/blog/boston/new-england-patriots/post/_/id/4683840/gillette-naming-rights-extended-through-2031 |url-status=live }}</ref> Athletes such as [[Roger Federer]],<ref>{{cite news |last1=Murray |first1=Tom |last2=Rogers |first2=Taylor Nicole |title=Roger Federer is the world's highest-paid athlete for the first time ever. Here's how he earned $106 million last year. |url=https://www.businessinsider.com/the-incredible-life-of-roger-federer-2017-1 |access-date=January 26, 2021 |work=[[Business Insider]] |quote=In 2007, he was signed by Gillette, starring in a number of ads for the company. |date=June 7, 2020 |archive-date=January 27, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210127221013/https://www.businessinsider.com/the-incredible-life-of-roger-federer-2017-1 |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Tiger Woods]],<ref>{{cite news |title=Gillette will not renew Tiger Woods |url=https://www.reuters.com/article/sports/gillette-will-not-renew-tiger-woods-idUSTRE6BM4IR/ |access-date=May 26, 2026 |publisher=Reuters |date=December 23, 2010 |archive-date=February 2, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210202223935/https://www.reuters.com/article/idINIndia-53762620101223 |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Shoaib Malik]],<ref name="Sport">{{cite book |last1=Thangaraj |first1=Stanley |last2=Burdsey |first2=Daniel |last3=Dudrah |first3=Rajinder |title=Sport and South Asian Diasporas: Playing through Time and Space |year=2015 |publisher=Routledge |page=29 |isbn=978-1317684299 |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=zKbbCgAAQBAJ&pg=PA29 |access-date=January 26, 2021 |quote=For instance, in an ad for Gillette razors, both Dravid and Malik seem reserved and dignified. This popular campaign, in which Gillette filmed identical segments of celebrity athletes strutting in black outfits, shaving, and giving each other knowing glances, presents both Dravid and Malik as antic-free and suave. |archive-date=September 2, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210902005128/https://books.google.com/books?id=zKbbCgAAQBAJ&pg=PA29 |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Derek Jeter]],<ref>{{cite news |last1=Reidy |first1=Chris |title=Gillette pays tribute to Derek Jeter |url=https://www.boston.com/uncategorized/noprimarytagmatch/2011/07/11/gillette-pays-tribute-to-derek-jeter/ |access-date=January 26, 2021 |work=[[Boston.com]] |date=July 11, 2011 |quote=New York Yankee star Jeter has long been a pitch-man for Gillette, the Boston-based razor-blade brand. |archive-date=February 3, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210203072117/https://www.boston.com/uncategorized/noprimarytagmatch/2011/07/11/gillette-pays-tribute-to-derek-jeter |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Thierry Henry]],<ref>{{cite news |last1=Parsons |first1=Russell |title=Gillette stands by Henry despite handball |url=https://www.marketingweek.com/gillette-stands-by-henry-despite-handball/ |access-date=January 26, 2021 |work=[[Marketing Week]] |date=November 20, 2009 |archive-date=February 3, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210203172029/https://www.marketingweek.com/gillette-stands-by-henry-despite-handball/ |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Kenan Sofuoğlu]],<ref>{{cite web |last1=Güncelleme |first1=Son |title=Dünya Şampiyonu Türk Sporcu, Gıllette Fusıon'un Reklam Filminde Yer Aldı |url=https://www.haberler.com/dunya-sampiyonu-turk-sporcu-gillette-fusion-un-haberi/ |website=Haberler.com |date=19 March 2008 |publisher=March 19, 2008 |access-date=January 26, 2021 |language=Turkish |archive-date=February 7, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210207213225/https://www.haberler.com/dunya-sampiyonu-turk-sporcu-gillette-fusion-un-haberi/ |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Park Ji-sung]],<ref>{{cite news |last1=Castles |first1=Duncan |title=Park Ji-sung's philosophy is simple – there is no 'I' in football |url=https://www.thenationalnews.com/sport/park-ji-sung-s-philosophy-is-simple-there-is-no-i-in-football-1.587869?videoId=5771275459001 |access-date=January 26, 2021 |work=[[The National (Abu Dhabi)|The National]] |date=May 22, 2011 |archive-date=September 2, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210902005128/https://www.thenationalnews.com/sport/park-ji-sung-s-philosophy-is-simple-there-is-no-i-in-football-1.587869?videoId=5771275459001 |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Rahul Dravid]],<ref>{{cite news |last1=Sen |first1=Debarati S. |title=Rahul Dravid recounts his first shave with his father at a Gillette event in Mumbai |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/events/mumbai/rahul-dravid-recounts-his-first-shave-with-his-father-at-a-gillette-event-in-mumbai/articleshow/36775102.cms |access-date=January 26, 2021 |work=[[The Times of India]] |date=June 19, 2014 |archive-date=June 23, 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140623141512/http://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/events/mumbai/Rahul-Dravid-recounts-his-first-shave-with-his-father-at-a-Gillette-event-in-Mumbai/articleshow/36775102.cms |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Raheem Sterling]],<ref>{{cite journal |last1=Delahunty |first1=Stephen |title=Watch: Raheem Sterling helps Gillette launch 'Made of What Matters' campaign |journal=[[PRWeek]] |date=February 11, 2020 |url=https://www.prweek.com/article/1673495/watch-raheem-sterling-helps-gillette-launch-made-matters-campaign |access-date=January 26, 2021 |archive-date=January 25, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210125105232/https://www.prweek.com/article/1673495/watch-raheem-sterling-helps-gillette-launch-made-matters-campaign |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Karl-Anthony Towns]],<ref>{{cite journal |last1=Amay |first1=Joane |title=NBA All-Star Karl-Anthony Towns Gives Us an Inside Look Into His Style Game |journal=[[Ebony (magazine)|Ebony]] |date=July 1, 2019 |url=https://www.ebony.com/ebony-magazine/nba-all-star-karl-anthony-towns-gives-us-an-inside-look-into-his-style-game/ |access-date=January 26, 2021 |quote=KAT, a Gillette celebrity brand ambassador, is also known for his off-court style prowess. |archive-date=January 20, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210120080140/https://www.ebony.com/ebony-magazine/nba-all-star-karl-anthony-towns-gives-us-an-inside-look-into-his-style-game/ |url-status=live }}</ref> and [[Michael Clarke (cricketer)|Michael Clarke]] have been sponsored by the company,<ref>{{cite news |title=Gillette won't renew contract with Woods |url=https://www.smh.com.au/world/gillette-wont-renew-contract-with-woods-20101224-196zp.html |access-date=January 26, 2021 |work=[[The Sydney Morning Herald]] |quote=The brand, owned by Procter & Gamble Co, used Woods, Roger Federer, Lionel Messi, Australian cricket vice-captain Michael Clarke and dozens of other athletes as part of its three-year "Gillette Champions" marketing campaign. |date=December 24, 2010 |archive-date=September 2, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210902005122/https://www.smh.com.au/world/gillette-wont-renew-contract-with-woods-20101224-196zp.html |url-status=live }}</ref> as well as video gaming personality [[Dr Disrespect]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/twitch-streamer-drdisrespect-signs-caa-1175330|title=CAA Signs Twitch Streamer DrDisrespect (Exclusive)|website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]|language=en|access-date=January 15, 2019|date=January 10, 2019|first=Natalie|last=Jarvey|archive-date=January 11, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190111041802/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/twitch-streamer-drdisrespect-signs-caa-1175330|url-status=live}}</ref>

In November 2009, Gillette became the subject of a proposed boycott in Ireland due to its endorsement by French soccer player Thierry Henry; his undetected handball foul during a [[2009 Republic of Ireland v France football matches|FIFA World Cup qualifying match]] contributed to a game-winning goal by France, eliminating Ireland from contention.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2009/nov/19/thierry-henry-france-football-worldcup|title=Hands-on Thierry Henry becomes public enemy numéro un|last=Ronay|first=Barney|date=2009-11-19|work=The Guardian|access-date=2019-01-15|language=en-GB|issn=0261-3077|archive-date=2020-08-11|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200811165149/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2009/nov/19/thierry-henry-france-football-worldcup|url-status=live}}</ref> The following month, expanding upon the controversy, media outlets observed a "[[Sports-related curses|curse]]" associated with top athletes who endorse Gillette, also citing Tiger Woods (who became the subject of an [[Tiger Woods#Infidelity scandal and fallout|infidelity scandal]] in late 2009), and Roger Federer losing in an upset to [[Nikolay Davydenko]] during the [[2009 ATP World Tour Finals]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.couriermail.com.au/sport/more-sports/the-kennett-curse-has-nothing-on-these-long-running-sporting-curses-from-around-the-world/news-story/1bf831664b7fa58817919571a5362f0a|title='Kennett Curse' has nothing on these|date=2013-09-18|website=Courier Mail|language=en|access-date=2019-01-15|archive-date=2020-12-26|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201226165840/https://www.couriermail.com.au/sport/more-sports/the-kennett-curse-has-nothing-on-these-long-running-sporting-curses-from-around-the-world/news-story/1bf831664b7fa58817919571a5362f0a?nk=79da522e77482a3515dec614badc8ce5-1609001920|url-status=live}}</ref>

Since its opening in 2002, Gillette has held [[naming rights]] to [[Gillette Stadium]] in nearby [[Foxborough]], home of the [[New England Patriots]] of the [[National Football League]] and the [[New England Revolution]] of [[Major League Soccer]]. The original agreement lasted through 2017; in 2010, P&G negotiated a 15-year extension, lasting through 2031.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.boston.com/sports/new-england-patriots/2010/09/22/naming-rights_d/|title=Naming-rights deal extended through 2031|date=2010-09-22|work=Boston.com|access-date=2019-01-15|language=en-US|archive-date=2020-11-29|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201129082927/https://www.boston.com/sports/extra-points/2010/09/22/naming-rights_d|url-status=live}}</ref>

Since the 1990s, the company has used a marketing list to send a [[free sample]] of a Gillette razor in promotional packages to men in celebration of their 18th birthday. The campaign has occasionally resulted in the samples accidentally being sent to recipients outside of the demographic, such as a 50-year-old woman.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2017/07/16/business/media/gillette-razors-marketing-mistakes.html|title=Welcome to Manhood, Gillette Told the 50-Year-Old Woman|last=Maheshwari|first=Sapna|date=2017-07-16|work=The New York Times|access-date=2019-01-15|language=en-US|issn=0362-4331|archive-date=2020-11-09|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201109030819/https://www.nytimes.com/2017/07/16/business/media/gillette-razors-marketing-mistakes.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.thegazette.com/subject/news/nation-and-world/retails-new-niche-aging-baby-boomers-20180831|title=Retail's new niche: Aging baby boomers|website=The Gazette|access-date=2019-01-15|archive-date=2020-08-10|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200810222112/https://www.thegazette.com/subject/news/nation-and-world/retails-new-niche-aging-baby-boomers-20180831|url-status=live}}</ref>

In 2019, Gillette and [[Twitch (service)|Twitch]] partnered to form the [[esports]] group Gillette Gaming Alliance, as well as the Bits for Blades campaign which gave Twitch Bits (the site's [[digital currency]]) to those who purchased Gillette products online. The 2019 team had eleven streamers, each representing a different country,<ref>{{cite journal |last1=Brunsman |first1=Barrett J. |title=P&G drafts video game team to boost brand with esports fans |journal=Cincinnati Business Courier |date=March 28, 2019 |url=https://www.bizjournals.com/cincinnati/news/2019/03/28/p-g-drafts-video-game-team-to-boost-brand-with.html |access-date=March 9, 2021 |archive-date=September 2, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210902005144/https://www.bizjournals.com/cincinnati/news/2019/03/28/p-g-drafts-video-game-team-to-boost-brand-with.html |url-status=live }}</ref> and the 2020 team had five streamers including [[DrLupo]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Takahashi |first1=Dean |title=Gillette and Twitch round up esports influencers in gaming alliance |url=https://venturebeat.com/2020/02/11/gillette-and-twitch-round-up-esports-influencers-in-gaming-alliance/ |access-date=March 9, 2021 |work=VentureBeat |date=February 11, 2020 |archive-date=January 26, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210126092736/https://venturebeat.com/2020/02/11/gillette-and-twitch-round-up-esports-influencers-in-gaming-alliance/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite journal |last1=Stam |first1=Aleda |title=How brands are getting into the Twitch game |journal=[[PRWeek]] |date=October 30, 2020 |url=https://www.prweek.com/article/1698820/brands-getting-twitch-game |access-date=March 9, 2021 |quote=When Gillette renewed its Gillette Gaming Alliance this year, the brand continued its Bits for Blades program, where Twitch users who buy Gillette products can enter a unique promo code at checkout and receive Twitch Bits in return. |archive-date=January 15, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210115184432/https://www.prweek.com/article/1698820/brands-getting-twitch-game |url-status=live }}</ref> During 2020–2021, Gillette enlisted NFL players [[Saquon Barkley]], [[Ashtyn Davis]], [[Jalen Hurts]], [[Cole Kmet]], and [[Tua Tagovailoa]] as brand ambassadors.<ref>{{cite journal |title=NFL Playbook: Tracking How Brands Are Marketing Around an Uncertain Season |journal=[[Ad Age]] |date=January 4, 2021 |url=https://adage.com/article/cmo-strategy/nfl-playbook-tracking-how-brands-are-marketing-around-uncertain-season/2279041 |access-date=March 9, 2021 |archive-date=March 2, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210302112016/https://adage.com/article/cmo-strategy/nfl-playbook-tracking-how-brands-are-marketing-around-uncertain-season/2279041 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite journal|url=https://www.bizjournals.com/tampabay/news/2021/01/25/super-bowl-lv-in-tampa-hospitality-reality.html|title=Super Bowl LV in Tampa: Hospitality reality|journal=Tampa Bay Business Journal|first=Terry|last=Lefton|date=January 25, 2021|quote=Gillette is hoping to do something on social media with its quintet of NFL endorsers: New York Giants running back Saquon Barkley, New York Jet safety Ashtyn Davis, Philadelphia Eagles quarterback Jalen Hurts, Chicago Bears tight end Cole Kmet and Miami Dolphins quarterback Tua Tagovailoa.|access-date=March 13, 2021|archive-date=January 26, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210126001008/https://www.bizjournals.com/tampabay/news/2021/01/25/super-bowl-lv-in-tampa-hospitality-reality.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

Gillette became the jersey sponsor of the [[New England Revolution]] in 2025.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.mlssoccer.com/news/new-england-revolution-add-gillette-as-official-jersey-sponsor|title=New England Revolution add Gillette as official jersey sponsor &#124; MLSSoccer.com|website=mlssoccer}}</ref>

== In science ==
In [[laser]] research and development, Gillette razor blades are used as a [[List of non-coherent units of measurement|non-standard measurement]] as a rough estimate of a particular laser beam's penetrative ability; a "four-Gillette laser", for example, can burn through four blades.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.wired.com/2011/12/st_3st_lasers/|title=Three Smart Things About Lasers|author=Rachel Zurer|magazine=Wired|date=December 27, 2011|access-date=May 21, 2015|archive-date=November 11, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201111210611/http://www.wired.com/2011/12/st_3st_lasers/|url-status=live}}</ref>

== In music ==
A Gillette razorblade was used as a tool to achieve a certain sound by the [[England|English]] [[Rock music|rock]] band [[The Kinks]]. Kinks member [[Dave Davies]] became "really bored with this guitar sound – or lack of an interesting sound" so he purchased "a little green amplifier{{nbsp}}...an Elpico" from a radio spares shop in [[Muswell Hill]],<ref>{{Cite web |title=Dave's Guitars and the Green Amp |url=http://www.davedavies.com/guitars/guitars2.htm |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160425162920/http://www.davedavies.com/guitars/guitars2.htm |url-status=dead |archive-date=2016-04-25 |website=davedavies.com}}</ref> and "twiddled around with it", including "taking the wires going to the speaker and putting a jack plug on there and plugging it straight into my [[AC30]]" (a larger amplifier), but did not get the sound he wanted until he got frustrated and "got a single-sided Gillette razorblade and cut round the cone [from the center to the edge]{{nbsp}}... so it was all shredded but still on there, still intact. I played and I thought it was amazing."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hunter |first=Dave |date=January 1999 |title=The Kinks Guitar Sound |url=http://www.davedavies.com/articles/tgm_0199-01.htm |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150712032915/http://www.davedavies.com/articles/tgm_0199-01.htm |url-status=dead |archive-date=2015-07-12 |website=Voxes, Vees And Razorblades |publisher=The Guitar Magazine |via=davedavies.com}}</ref> The sound was replicated in the studio by having the Elpico plugged into the Vox AC30. It was this sound, courtesy of a Gillette razor blade that became a mainstay on many of The Kinks early recordings, including "[[You Really Got Me]]" and "[[All Day and All of the Night]]".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Erlewine |first=Stephen Thomas |title=The Kinks |url=https://www.allmusic.com/artist/the-kinks-mn0000100160 |website=Biography |publisher=All Music |access-date=2019-07-29 |archive-date=2012-06-02 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120602040246/https://www.allmusic.com/artist/the-kinks-mn0000100160 |url-status=live }}</ref>

== Operations in Canada ==
In late 1988, Gillette announced plans to eliminate manufacturing operations in Montreal and Toronto. The Canadian unit's executive offices remained in Montreal, with administrative, distribution, marketing, and sales operations continuing in both cities. Approximately 600 employees in Canada were laid off as part of the global restructuring,<ref>{{cite news |title=Gillette Plans to Phase Out Canada Plants |url=https://www.chicagotribune.com/news/ct-xpm-1988-11-24-8802190240-story.html |access-date=October 22, 2020 |work=[[Chicago Tribune]] |date=November 24, 1988 |archive-date=September 2, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210902005124/https://www.chicagotribune.com/ |url-status=live }}</ref> which followed a $720 million [[share repurchase]] and sought to "rationalize worldwide production".<ref name="Burns">{{cite news |last1=Burns |first1=John F. |title=Canada Girds for Action on Trade Bill |url=https://www.nytimes.com/1988/11/24/world/canada-girds-for-action-on-trade-bill.html |access-date=October 22, 2020 |work=[[The New York Times]] |date=November 24, 1988 |archive-date=January 8, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210108130228/https://www.nytimes.com/1988/11/24/world/canada-girds-for-action-on-trade-bill.html |url-status=live }}</ref> As of 2005, Gillette was not producing products in Canada and employed approximately 200 people in Edmonton, Mississauga, and Montreal.<ref>{{cite news |title=P&G cuts mega-deal with Gillette |url=https://www.theglobeandmail.com/report-on-business/pg-cuts-mega-deal-with-gillette/article4114805/ |access-date=October 29, 2020 |work=[[The Globe and Mail]] |date=January 29, 2005 |first1=Barrie |last1=McKenna |first2=Virginia |last2=Galt |archive-date=October 29, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201029153501/https://www.theglobeandmail.com/report-on-business/pg-cuts-mega-deal-with-gillette/article4114805/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

